       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Higher doses haven't been shown to work better, and they raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and seizures. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **A dose-entry error.** Common intended doses are 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg once daily. Titration usually starts at 25\u201350 mg and goes up in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least one week.\n- **A deliberate supratherapeutic dose.** Tell me and I can enter it with a note recording your rationale, such as a specialist recommendation or a documented plan for monitoring. Many hospitals also require pharmacy review for doses above the maximum.\n\nTell me the dose and any note you want on the order, and I'll enter it."
      }
